    "title": "What time will Artemis II return? How to watch splash down in Arizona",
    "text": "Updated April 10, 2026, 4:40 p.m. MTThe Artemis II mission is scheduled to splash down on Friday, April 10, at 5:07 p.m. Arizona time.NASA's four-person crew completed a 10-day mission around the moon aboard the Orion spacecraft.The spacecraft will splash down in the Pacific Ocean near the coast of San Diego.Zero gravity chaos, a jar of Nutella floating around, exercise routines and morning wake-up songs to add to our playlists.These are just a few of the highlights that the Artemis II crew gave us during their 10-day mission around the moon. The crew of four astronauts launches aboard the Orion to travel farther than any human has gone before. Along the way, the crew has tested navigation systems, life support, radiation protection and more.As the grand tour wraps up and the mission proves to be successful, it's time for these astronauts to come home. Here is everything to know about when Artemis II will splash down.What time will artemis 2 splash down?NASA's Artemis II mission is splashing down at 5:07 p.m., Arizona time, on Friday, April 10.Will splashdown be televised?Yes, the Artemis II splashdown will be televised and streamed live. Coverage of the Orion capsule's return will be available on NASA+, the NASA app and the NASA YouTube channel.Where will Artemis II splashdown?NASA says the Orion spacecraft will splash down in the Pacific Ocean off the San Diego coast.Got a story you want to share? Reach out at Tiffany.Acosta@gannett.com. Follow @tiffsario on Instagram.Looking for thebest things to do in Arizona? Sign up for our newsletter.",
